Chapter: GuardStr

 A TEXT LITERAL IN A MATCH-BRANCH GUARD. `collect-strings-branches-loop` walks
 each branch's BODY and never its guard, so a literal that appears only in a
 guard never reaches the string table. `strtab-lookup` answers 0 for a miss, so
 the comparison runs against address zero and quietly fails.

 The literals are built at run time -- `"zeb" & "ra"` -- so constant folding
 cannot turn the comparison into a decision the emitter makes for itself.

 Expected, and what the zig plug prints: yes, then no.

  Box =
    | Boxed (Text)

  classify : Text -> Text
  classify (v) =
   when Boxed v
    is Boxed (x) when x == "zebra" -> "yes"
    is otherwise -> "no"

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (classify ("zeb" & "ra"))
    print-line-uni (classify ("no" & "pe"))
  end
